    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -460,
        "y": 0
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Two checkpoints of one run, scored on the same test split: after epoch 1 (digits-epoch1.pt) and after epoch 15 (digits-epoch15.pt). Each is loaded into a fresh SequentialModel, so this is how you would compare checkpoints from two different runs too. Test accuracy goes from 0.740 to 0.962. The script lists the images the two label differently: 109 test images change label, the later checkpoint fixes 100 of them and breaks 0.\n\n同一次訓練的兩個 checkpoint，用同一份測試資料評分：第 1 個 epoch 之後（digits-epoch1.pt）與第 15 個 epoch 之後（digits-epoch15.pt）。兩個都載入全新的 SequentialModel，所以比較兩次不同訓練的 checkpoint 也是這樣做。測試正確率從 0.740 變成 0.962。腳本列出兩者標成不同數字的影像：109 張測試影像的標籤改變，後面的 checkpoint 修正其中 100 張、弄錯 0 張。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -460,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 380
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-compare",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 4305,
        "y": -480
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "The two orange bubbles are Compare segments, one from load-early to infer-early and one from load-late to infer-late. After a run, click the orange border of a bubble and the Inspector lists what goes into that segment (the loaded model and the test images) and what comes out (the predicted scores). To add your own: select two nodes (click one, Shift-click the other), open Settings (the gear in the toolbar) and under Recording & Inspection click Create segment.\n\n兩個橘色泡泡是「段落比較」，一個從 load-early 到 infer-early，一個從 load-late 到 infer-late。執行之後，點泡泡的橘色邊框，Inspector 會列出進入這一段的東西（載入的模型與測試影像）和出來的東西（預測分數）。要自己加一段：選取兩個節點（點一個，再按住 Shift 點另一個），打開「設定」（工具列的齒輪），在「錄製與檢視」下按「建立段落」。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "load-early",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -480
        },
        "noteWidth": 340
      }
